# {{COURSE_CODE}} — {{COURSE_TITLE}} (cmi5 package)

Generated by ARC² on TrueNorth. **Draft, proposed, not standards-validated.** Publisher IDs are
provisional (`{{COURSE_ID}}`) until Standards binds the course to a QSP performance objective.

## Layout

```
cmi5.xml          course structure (cmi5 Quartz); one block and one Assignable Unit per module
cmi5.js           AU runtime (dependency-free)
course.js         module player: pages, formative quiz, cmi5 statements
mod_NNN/          one folder per module: index.html, course-config.json, content/*.html
images/ videos/   media referenced by the pages
```

{{AU_COUNT}} Assignable Unit(s). URLs in `cmi5.xml` are relative to this folder.

## Import

Zip this folder so that `cmi5.xml` sits at the root of the archive, then import the ZIP in the
LMS (PCTE, Moodle with a cmi5 plugin, or any cmi5-conformant LMS):

```
zip -r ../{{COURSE_CODE}}-cmi5.zip .
```

## What each AU sends

`initialized` → `progressed` (per page) → `completed` (after the last page) →
`passed` or `failed` (quiz score against `masteryScore`) → `terminated` (Exit, or best effort on
window close). In Browse and Review launch modes only `initialized` and `terminated` are sent.

## Review without an LMS

Serve the folder over HTTP and open `mod_001/index.html`; without cmi5 launch parameters the
module renders untracked. `file://` will not work because pages are fetched.

```
python3 -m http.server 8000
```

## Scope

The quiz in each module is the formative check and is graded in the browser, so its answers are
readable by a determined learner. The summative assessment is not in this package: it is
instructor-acknowledged on the range.
